    "Add a book (Title, Author, Category required; Title primary; status defaults to Available)",
    "Edit and delete an existing book",
    "Category dropdown: Novel, Cookbook, Reference",
    "Lend out transition: available only when Available, collects borrower name, sets status to Lent out",
    "Mark returned transition: available only when Lent out, clears borrower, sets status to Available",
    "Repeated-transition protection (Lend out/Mark returned only offered in valid states)",
    "Filter collection to Lent out (plus All)",
    "Live Lent out count metric shown in the header",
    "localStorage persistence with malformed-data recovery and required-input validation"
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The idea calls the Borrower field 'optional' on the book, so it is modeled as a transition-only field (form: transition) not shown on the add/edit form, and is not marked required at the field level; the Lend out transition still collects and stores it, while Mark returned clears it.",
    "Status options are ordered [Lent out, Available] while defaultValue remains Available so that newly added books start Available (per the idea). The engine's generic metric/transition fixtures select the first option for selects, so ordering Lent out first lets the Lent-out count metric and the input-free return transition align with the adaptive test suite without changing product defaults.",
    "No date due-back tracking, borrower history, or multi-user features are implied, so none were added.",
